# Routing gate

coach-hq is a multi-agent repo. Five agents share it and you are exactly ONE of them.

**Before any tool call, git command, PR/issue triage or boot sequence:** read
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) → "Agent Routing" and follow it. That section is the single
source for the table, the HQ default, and the watch-out about what does *not* decide
your role. It is not restated here — one copy, so the copies cannot disagree
(`kdb/decisions/0031-enforcement-lives-in-git-and-ci-not-agent-hooks.md`).

Read it even when the session looks obviously like engineering work. Looking obvious is
the failure mode the gate exists to catch.
